      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1352110099,
      "text": "Bambusa bambos, the giant thorny bamboo, Indian thorny bamboo, spiny bamboo, or thorny bamboo is a species of clumping bamboo native to southern Asia. It is also naturalized in Seychelles, Central America, West Indies, Java, Malaysia, Maluku, and the Philippines."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Bambusa bambos",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bambusa_bambos",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 175742022,
      "text": "El bambú de la India, mambú de la India o caña brava asiática es una especie de bambú perteneciente a la familia de las poáceas."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Bambusa bambos",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bambusa_bambos",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 224325221,
      "text": "Bambusa bambos, le bambou épineux, est une espèce de plantes monocotylédones de la famille des Poaceae, sous-famille des Bambusoideae, originaire du sud de l'Asie."
    }
